{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>To offer their sacrifices to YHWH in the wilderness of Sinai.</b> For they offered no sacrifice until they came to Mount Sinai. I have already shown you that the altar Moses built on the weakness of Amalek is at Horeb, and it is Mount Sinai. There Israel stayed a year minus ten days, as it is written. And in the wilderness they did not offer burnt offerings, as the prophet said: \"The sacrifices and meal-offerings that you brought Me in the wilderness forty years, O house of Israel.\" They also did not make the Passover except in Egypt and a second time at Mount Sinai, for in the wilderness they had no livestock. And after they departed from Mount Sinai they did not circumcise on the way, and behold, most of them were uncircumcised; and on account of eating the Passover Joshua circumcised them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:59.724781921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}